1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,500
Don't worry, Alexandra.

2
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:03,818
We'll find the owner.

3
00:00:03,818 --> 00:00:05,658
How, Robbie?

4
00:00:05,658 --> 00:00:06,456
Let me think.

5
00:00:06,456 --> 00:00:07,289
Gemma, sit.

6
00:00:07,289 --> 00:00:07,956
Good Gemma.

7
00:00:07,956 --> 00:00:10,434
Give me your paw.

8
00:00:10,434 --> 00:00:11,912
Good Gemma.

9
00:00:11,912 --> 00:00:13,912
This dog is well trained.

10
00:00:13,912 --> 00:00:14,890
She likes you, too.

11
00:00:14,890 --> 00:00:16,890
So how are we going to find the owners?

12
00:00:16,890 --> 00:00:20,846
With a little help from the ASPCA,

13
00:00:20,846 --> 00:00:24,366
the American Society for the Prevention of Cruelty to Animals.

14
00:00:24,366 --> 00:00:25,993
They're the ones.

15
00:00:25,993 --> 00:00:26,802
We once found a cat.

16
00:00:26,802 --> 00:00:29,052
She was caught in the branches of our tree.

17
00:00:29,052 --> 00:00:30,510
And Dad called the ASPCA.

18
00:00:30,510 --> 00:00:32,758
They came and solved the problem.

19
00:00:32,758 --> 00:00:38,714
Robbie, let's call them.

20
00:00:38,714 --> 00:00:44,669
Let me see -- ASPCA...

21
00:00:44,669 --> 00:00:47,647
Here it is.

22
00:00:47,647 --> 00:00:53,603
ASPCA Animal Shelter.

23
00:00:53,603 --> 00:01:02,537
555-7700.

24
00:01:02,537 --> 00:01:08,493
Hello, ASPCA.

25
00:01:08,493 --> 00:01:12,671
Hello, my name is Robbie Stewart.

26
00:01:12,671 --> 00:01:15,302
I have a lost dog I'd like to bring to you.

27
00:01:15,302 --> 00:01:16,479
How late are you open?

28
00:01:16,479 --> 00:01:18,427
We're open till nine P.M.

29
00:01:18,427 --> 00:01:19,427
Thank you.

30
00:01:19,427 --> 00:01:20,405
I'll bring the dog over by nine.

31
00:01:20,405 --> 00:01:21,085
Thanks.

32
00:01:21,085 --> 00:01:21,765
Bye.

33
00:01:21,765 --> 00:01:23,383
Thanks.

34
00:01:23,383 --> 00:01:32,317
Good-bye.

35
00:01:32,317 --> 00:01:33,277
They're still open?

36
00:01:33,277 --> 00:01:34,877
They're open until nine o'clock.

37
00:01:34,877 --> 00:01:36,495
We have two and a half hours.

38
00:01:36,495 --> 00:01:38,849
Let's take Gemma by there now.

39
00:01:38,849 --> 00:01:41,251
They'll find the owner.

40
00:01:41,251 --> 00:01:42,251
I hope so.

41
00:01:42,251 --> 00:01:45,869
I'm so sad to see this little dog without her family.

42
00:01:45,869 --> 00:01:47,207
I'm sure they'll find the owner.

43
00:01:47,207 --> 00:01:50,185
But if they don't, I'll adopt her.

44
00:01:50,185 --> 00:01:53,163
She's so cute.

45
00:01:53,163 --> 00:01:56,140
Look at those eyes.

46
00:01:56,140 --> 00:01:59,118
She's hard to resist.

47
00:01:59,118 --> 00:02:02,096
Don't you just love her?

48
00:02:02,096 --> 00:02:05,074
I'd like to keep her, too.

49
00:02:05,074 --> 00:02:06,689
But I'll be going home to Greece

50
00:02:06,689 --> 00:02:08,052
at the end of the semester.

51
00:02:08,052 --> 00:02:11,030
She just wants love and affection.

52
00:02:11,030 --> 00:02:14,675
Come on, Robbie.

53
00:02:14,675 --> 00:02:16,986
Let's get her to the animal shelter,

54
00:02:16,986 --> 00:02:19,964
so they can find her owners quickly.

55
00:02:19,964 --> 00:02:21,164
Don't worry, Gemma.

56
00:02:21,164 --> 00:02:22,942
We'll get you home.

57
00:02:22,942 --> 00:02:25,920
It's not easy being away from home.

58
00:02:25,920 --> 00:02:27,627
Come on, poochie.

59
00:02:27,627 --> 00:02:28,898
Atta girl!

60
00:02:28,898 --> 00:02:30,898
Let's go.

61
00:02:30,898 --> 00:02:55,700
We're off to the animal shelter.

62
00:02:55,700 --> 00:02:57,700
Your name?

63
00:02:57,700 --> 00:02:58,678
Robbie Stewart.

64
00:02:58,678 --> 00:03:01,656
And this is Alexandra Pappas.

65
00:03:01,656 --> 00:03:04,634
Your name will do, Mr. Stewart.

66
00:03:04,634 --> 00:03:07,612
Your address?

67
00:03:07,612 --> 00:03:13,567
46 Linden street, Riverdale.

68
00:03:13,567 --> 00:03:16,829
Where did you find the dog?

69
00:03:16,829 --> 00:03:17,681
She found us.

70
00:03:17,681 --> 00:03:20,380
You tried calling the number on the collar?

71
00:03:20,380 --> 00:03:23,439
Yes, but the number's no longer in service.

72
00:03:23,439 --> 00:03:26,979
And there's no address on the dog tag?

73
00:03:26,979 --> 00:03:29,441
There's no other information.

74
00:03:29,441 --> 00:03:32,393
No ID number.

75
00:03:32,393 --> 00:03:32,935
Without that, it's hard.

76
00:03:32,935 --> 00:03:36,461
You will try to find the dog's owner.

77
00:03:36,461 --> 00:03:38,171
Oh, we'll try, believe me.

78
00:03:38,171 --> 00:03:40,369
And if you don't?

79
00:03:40,369 --> 00:03:42,369
Yes?

80
00:03:42,369 --> 00:03:46,325
If you don't ... can I ... can I adopt the dog?

81
00:03:46,325 --> 00:03:47,555
Why, yes.

82
00:03:47,555 --> 00:03:50,658
If the owners don't claim the dog in forty-eight hours,

83
00:03:50,658 --> 00:03:52,281
then you can apply for adoption.

84
00:03:52,281 --> 00:03:54,001
How do I do that?

85
00:03:54,001 --> 00:03:55,259
You really want to?

86
00:03:55,259 --> 00:03:56,384
Yes, I'm serious.

87
00:03:56,384 --> 00:03:59,083
If no one comes to claim Gemma,

88
00:03:59,083 --> 00:04:01,215
I'd like to adopt her.

89
00:04:01,215 --> 00:04:02,215
It's not difficult.
